This is similar to that:
http://stackoverflow.com/questions/13649562/rpy2-importr-failing-with-xts-and-quantmod

The "automagic" translation of "." in R names into "_" ("." is not a 
valid character for variable names in Python) in rpy2 is reporting a 
conflict. Here is it trying to convert the name "read.mtp" into 
"read_mtp", but "read_mtp" is already present in the package "foreign".

